35,2,1,talk,Toshio,,The post-occupancy data is clear. Projects that serve many departments are rated highest. Single-wing benefits are ignored.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Victoria,,My findings show that taking rooms out of service forces us to pay for off-site space for two terms. It is a hidden cost.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,"The staffing data is grim. Front-of-house posts are unfilled, but technicians have spare hours. We are misallocating labor.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"The site diaries show six weeks lost to weather. The survey findings reveal hazardous materials in older blocks, adding months of delay.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,Tender records show mechanical plant costs rose by a fifth. The renewal reserve for AV kit was never opened. We are underfunded.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Benjamin, your cost data aligns with my delivery findings. Inspection-driven works finish on time; comfort-driven ones slip.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Toshio, that explains the delays. But the booking data shows specialist rooms are idle, while general rooms are always full.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,"@Victoria, if general rooms are full, why are we building more specialist ones? The technicians are already overworked with manual checks.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, the weather risk is high for outdoor work. The survey delays in older blocks make any renovation there a nightmare.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mizuki, the survey delays confirm my fears. The market is punishing us for ignoring the physical reality of the buildings.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Victoria, the booking data is crucial. We should prioritize spaces that are actually used. The study commons fits this.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Toshio, I agree. The study commons avoids the off-site costs of closing labs. It uses existing space efficiently.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,George,,"@Toshio, the study commons requires minimal new staffing. The existing technicians can handle the basic upkeep without extra burden.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
